Chapter 1
Calling cards

— Dayna —

I could see the electrical impulses moving through the cords of my brain matter. I watched them alit with a sense of boundless joy and delayed confusion. Shades of red and blue and purple formed patterns of geometry in what I could only imagine was similar to the worlds Mike Lesky told Miss Darby’s grade 12 class after his weekend DMT experience.

But I am not high, this i know. I am sober, asleep in my bed, yet my vision is awake and it’s watching these shapes burst and form, twist and race, shape and reshape in a elegant dance of electricity and I can only think one thing: we are going to be alright.

This is not the first